The code statements that lead to the bug are:
list_del_rcu(&pnd->list);
kfree(pnd);
Reason:
`list_del_rcu()` removes the object from the RCU-protected list, but RCU readers may still hold references to the removed object. The subsequent `kfree()` immediately frees the memory, causing a slab-use-after-free when an RCU reader accesses the freed object.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
kfree_rcu(pnd, rcu);
Reason:
`kfree_rcu()` defers freeing the object until after an RCU grace period, ensuring that all RCU readers have completed their access before the memory is released, thus preventing the use-after-free.

